&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;http://apollo.io/&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-7a57a4e3-9668-4c92-9fb1-a9318bf3a91b--723603012&quot;&gt;Apollo.io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the leading go-to-market solution for revenue teams, trusted by over 500,000 companies and millions of users globally, from rapidly growing startups to some of the world&#39;s largest enterprises. Founded in 2015, the company is one of the fastest growing companies in SaaS, raising approximately $250 million to date and valued at $1.6 billion. &lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;http://apollo.io/&quot; data-token-index=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-7a57a4e3-9668-4c92-9fb1-a9318bf3a91b--723603012&quot;&gt;Apollo.io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; provides sales and marketing teams with easy access to verified contact data for over 210 million B2B contacts and 35 million companies worldwide, along with tools to engage and convert these contacts in one unified platform. By helping revenue professionals find the most accurate contact information and automating the outreach process, &lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;http://apollo.io/&quot; data-token-index=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-7a57a4e3-9668-4c92-9fb1-a9318bf3a91b--723603012&quot;&gt;Apollo.io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; turns prospects into customers.&amp;nbsp;Apollo raised a series D in 2023 and is backed by top-tier investors, including Sequoia Capital, Bain Capital Ventures, and more, and counts the former President and COO of Hubspot, JD Sherman, among its board members.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Enablement &amp;amp; the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enablement exists to be a strategic partner to our GTM roles—building role proficiency through clear, scalable programs that align to business priorities. We drive accountability and adoption so teams execute with confidence, deliver exceptional customer experiences, and achieve our revenue outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Global Revenue Onboarding Program Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll own Apollo’s global 30/60/90-day Revenue onboarding and ramp program. Your customer is anyone entering a “new seat”—whether through external hiring, an internal move or promotion, or an acquisition—across AE, AM, BDR, Solutions Consulting, and GTM Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll take an established program and evolve it into a world-class onboarding experience that is hands-on, role-relevant, measurable, and connected to what new hires are expected to do on the job. This role combines program management with performance enablement: success is measured by &lt;strong&gt;readiness, proficiency, and time to productivity.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;self-starter, builder, and creative innovator &lt;/strong&gt;who doesn’t wait to be told what to do. You see opportunities, bring forward ideas, and move with precision and intent to turn them into reality. You’re comfortable independently running a complex global program, setting the plan, driving decisions, and holding yourself and others accountable to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most importantly, &lt;strong&gt;you love the new-hire experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll be one of the first faces of Apollo Revenue for our new hires and set the tone for their journey. You care deeply about making people feel welcomed, connected, confident, and equipped to succeed—and you bring the energy, creativity, and operational rigor to make that experience exceptional at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the global onboarding journey.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the end-to-end 30/60/90-day program across Revenue roles and regions, creating one integrated experience that builds common GTM foundations before branching into role-specific learning at the right moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and measure readiness.&lt;/strong&gt; Establish learning outcomes, weekly milestones, assessments, certifications, and clear proficiency signals. Partner with Revenue Operations to connect learning progress with behavior, activity, and leading performance indicators and provide leaders visibility into ramp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build learning that reflects the job.&lt;/strong&gt; Create hands-on curricula and learning paths centered on practice, application, and feedback. Partner with Field Enablement to translate complex product, methodology, and GTM concepts into role-specific behaviors and connect onboarding to ongoing development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make managers part of the system.&lt;/strong&gt; Build clear manager expectations, coaching moments, tools, and readiness signals into the first 90 days. New-hire success is shared accountability; design the program to make that ownership visible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch a global New Hire Buddy Program.&lt;/strong&gt; Build a peer-to-peer learning program that helps new hires navigate Apollo, build relationships, and accelerate productivity while creating meaningful development opportunities for existing Revenue team members. Distribute new-hire learning and support across Enablement, managers, teams, and buddies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead a global, cross-functional program.&lt;/strong&gt; Orchestrate Field Enablement, Product, Product Marketing, Revenue Operations, managers, and SMEs to keep content current and credible. Deliver globally across the Americas and EMEA, leveraging regional partners to scale while maintaining consistent standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build an AI-forward learning experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI where it makes learners measurably better—from personalized learning and practice to faster feedback and scalable content. Continuously evaluate emerging AI and learning technology to keep Apollo’s onboarding experience modern and effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to the learner.&lt;/strong&gt; Facilitate foundational learning and maintain a direct connection to new hires and managers. Use their experience, feedback, and performance data to continuously improve the program you own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onboarding &amp;amp; program expertise.&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of experience in Revenue/Sales Enablement, onboarding, learning program management, or a related GTM role, ideally in SaaS or a high-growth environment. You’ve owned or meaningfully evolved an onboarding program before and can apply those lessons here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional operational discipline.&lt;/strong&gt; Highly organized and rigorous about project plans, timelines, dependencies, and follow-through. You thrive on turning a complex, multifaceted global program into a simple, well-orchestrated experience for learners, managers, and partners—and you don’t let details or commitments fall through the cracks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance orientation.&lt;/strong&gt; You think beyond completion rates and learner satisfaction. You know how to define proficiency and connect learning to readiness, behavior, ramp, and business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning architecture.&lt;/strong&gt; You have experience building role-based curricula, learning paths, assessments, certifications, and hands-on experiences that translate complex concepts into practical on-the-job behaviors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong program leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; You can bring structure to complexity, manage multiple audiences and workstreams, and influence stakeholders and SMEs across Sales, Product, Marketing, Operations, and Enablement without formal authority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; technology fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; You have hands-on experience using AI and modern learning technology to improve how people learn, practice, receive feedback, and build proficiency—and you actively explore new tools and approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manager &amp;amp; field partnership.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand the role frontline managers and Field Enablement play in successful ramp and know how to build accountability, coaching, and reinforcement into the learner journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilitation &amp;amp; communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re as comfortable designing the program as you are facilitating with new hires, communicating with leaders, and turning complex information into clear, engaging learning experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Builder mindset.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re energized by taking something that already works, identifying where it can be better, and evolving it as the business scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The listed Pay Range reflects the total cash compensation inclusive of annual base salary and annual bonus as applicable. For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonus target and annual base salary for the role. This salary range may be inclusive of several career levels at Apollo and will be narrowed during the interview process based on a number of factors, including the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and location. Applicants interested in this role who are not located in the US may request the annual salary range for their location during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity; company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; at least 10 paid holidays per year, flex PTO, and parental leave; employee assistance program and wellbeing benefits; global travel coverage; life/AD&amp;amp;D/STD/LTD insurance; FSA/HSA and medical, dental, and vision benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$125,600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$157,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;We are AI Native&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apollo.io is an AI-native company built on a culture of continuous improvement. We’re on the front lines of driving productivity for our customers—and we expect the same mindset from our team. If you&#39;re energized by finding smarter, faster ways to get things done using AI and automation, you&#39;ll thrive here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why You’ll Love Working at Apollo&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Apollo, we’re driven by a shared mission: to help our customers unlock their full revenue potential. That’s why we &lt;strong&gt;take extreme ownership&lt;/strong&gt; of our work, &lt;strong&gt;move with focus and urgency&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;learn voraciously&lt;/strong&gt; to stay ahead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest deeply in your growth, ensuring you have the resources, support, and autonomy to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;own your role and make a real impact&lt;/strong&gt;. Collaboration is at our core—we’re &lt;strong&gt;all for one&lt;/strong&gt;, meaning you’ll have a team across departments ready to help you succeed. We encourage &lt;strong&gt;bold ideas and courageous action&lt;/strong&gt;, giving you the freedom to experiment, take smart risks, and drive big wins.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for a place where your work matters, where you can push boundaries, and where your career can thrive—Apollo is the place for you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.apollo.io/we-are-apollo&quot;&gt;here!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

